// Boss pets - miniature followers for the King Black Dragon, the Kalphite Queen, the Giant Mole and
// the three Dagannoth Kings.
//
// ERA NOTE, stated once and deliberately: boss pets are a 2015-16 Old School feature, about a decade
// after this server's 2006 target. Everything else in this repo has been kept era-accurate; this is
// the first knowing anachronism and it was asked for.
//
// Each pet is the boss's own models at pet scale. size=1 so they path like a cat rather than a boss,
// resizeh/resizev shrunk from whatever the boss used, vislevel=hide, and no combat stats at all -
// these are followers, not monsters, and giving them stats would make them attackable.
//
// timer=20 matters. It is what makes [ai_timer,_bosspet] fire, which is the logic that teleports a
// pet back to its owner when it falls behind or the owner changes floor. NOT ONE of the cache's own
// petcat npcs sets it - kittenpet_*, growncat_* and overgrowncat_* all omit it - so [ai_timer,_petcat]
// in quest_fluffs/scripts/pet.rs2 has never fired for any cat in the game. Recorded rather than
// changed here; fixing cats is a separate call.
//
// The op set mirrors the cats: op1=Pick-up, op3=Talk-to. The cats' op4=Interact-with (shoo away) is
// deliberately left off - a pet you can pick up does not also need a way to lose it permanently.
//
// follower=yes is on every record here, and on every other npc in the tree that carries
// param=pet_item_id - the skilling pets, the metamorphosis forms, the kraken and the cats in
// _unpack/377/all.npc. It is one flag for the two things Old School does with a pet and this
// server was doing with neither:
//
//   * NO MINIMAP DOT. A follower was drawing the same yellow npc dot as a goblin. OSRS sets the
//     cache's own "no minimap" flag on all of them (npc 6636 Prince Black Dragon, 6651 Baby Mole,
//     5591 Kitten ... all carry opcode 93), and follower=yes sets it here.
//   * THE OPS ARE THE OWNER'S. Every op script in npc/scripts already refused a pet that was not
//     yours, but the options were still in everyone's right-click menu. OSRS took them out of it
//     on 15 May 2014: "The options on other players' pets are no longer visible." The client does
//     that now - see Client.addNpcOptions and the [follower_uid] varp it reads.

[bosspet_kbd]
name=Prince black dragon
desc=The biggest, meanest dragon around. Eventually.
model1=npc_king_dragon_1
model2=npc_king_dragon_2
model3=npc_king_dragon_3
model4=npc_king_dragon_4
model5=npc_king_dragon_5
head1=npc_bosspet_kbd_head1
size=1
resizeh=40
resizev=40
walkanim=osrs_seq_4635
readyanim=osrs_seq_90
vislevel=hide
timer=1
op1=Pick-up
op3=Talk-to
category=bosspet
follower=yes
param=pet_item_id,bosspet_kbd_item

[bosspet_kalphite_queen]
name=Kalphite princess
desc=I don't think insect repellent will work on her either.
model1=npc_bosspet_kalphite_queen_1
model2=npc_bosspet_kalphite_queen_2
model3=npc_bosspet_kalphite_queen_3
head1=npc_bosspet_kalphite_queen_head1
size=1
resizeh=45
resizev=45
walkanim=osrs_seq_6236
readyanim=osrs_seq_6236
vislevel=hide
timer=1
op1=Pick-up
op3=Talk-to
op4=Metamorphosis
category=bosspet
follower=yes
param=pet_item_id,bosspet_kalphite_queen_item
param=metamorph_next,bosspet_kalphite_queen_green

// The one pet that never was a shrunk boss: the 377 cache ships its own baby mole, and this used
